# Fast checks only. A slow commit hook gets bypassed with --no-verify within a
# week, and then it protects nothing. Linting the whole project takes ~18s, so
# lint-staged narrows it to the files actually being committed.
#
# The real gate is CI on the pull request; this exists to catch cheap mistakes
# before they cost a round trip.
pnpm exec lint-staged

# Not scopable to staged files — tsc needs the whole project to resolve types.
# ~4s, and it is the check that would have caught the 24 errors this repo
# accumulated while nothing was verifying them.
pnpm typecheck
